      "writtenOn": "2021-03-25T12:19:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suspect that you might be right. There are a few ways we can enforce this:\n\n1. Add a PREUPLOAD.cfg check which restricts the files this can be used to tests, testing.go files and a limited number of others. ATM that list is just:\n* android/test_asserts.go\n\nThe disadvantage of this approach is that it won\u0027t detect indirect call.\n\n2. Add some way to identify \"in a test\" and have it fail if that is not set. This would most likely need to modify the boilerplate to call a common function to run the tests that sets a global variable.\n\n3. Rename it to \"RelativeToTopForTestsOnlyPleaseDontUseElsewhere\" which might just work ;)",
      "parentUuid": "d7cce743_0f71072f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 178,
        "startChar": 64,
        "endLine": 178,
        "endChar": 96
      },
      "revId": "045c333c2c80833a904eb1036b68334f7e2dde43",
