      "writtenOn": "2021-03-25T13:29:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Testing objects that are shared typically live in testing.go files and they are still visible to runtime code.\n\nI have updated this with a proof of concept check that detects when run outside the test environment. A bit hacky as it checks command line args but it seems as though this is a `standard` way of detecting the test environment.",
      "parentUuid": "1122ac4f_e8249ede",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 178,
        "startChar": 64,
        "endLine": 178,
        "endChar": 96
      },
      "revId": "045c333c2c80833a904eb1036b68334f7e2dde43",
