        "id": 1066075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-25T10:58:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You mean specifically \"out/\" string?\n\nIn this case, it\u0027s dangerous because it works well in the default case when $OUT_DIR is not set but fail miserably when one does set $OUT_DIR. \n\nHow about adding a helper method instead that is called, dunno, CanonicalPathForTesting() whose receiver is one of the objects that only tests have access to?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 191,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 191,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "045c333c2c80833a904eb1036b68334f7e2dde43",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c9f6f630_06af063a",
        "filename": "android/paths.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 191,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-25T12:19:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve done that in a couple of places, NormalizePathForTesting, AssertPathRelativeToTopEquals, .... and it always results in a lot of noise in tests.\n\nAll this work on paths is to allow me to fix TestingBuildParams (which is a test only class) so that it always uses relative paths which would eliminate 90% of the noise in tests (there are other places they can get an absolute Path).\n\nBy dangerous you mean in the case when someone accidentally uses this in production code it will work in normal builds but break when OUT_DIR is set? I think that will be detected in presubmit. However, preventing its use outside tests would avoid that.",
      "parentUuid": "cd7d1268_1d761466",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 191,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 191,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "045c333c2c80833a904eb1036b68334f7e2dde43",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b58529d_ed7524ae",
        "filename": "android/paths.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 191,
      "author": {
        "id": 1066075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-25T13:00:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yep, that\u0027s the exact scenario I\u0027m worried about: that Soong works differently when OUT_DIR is set than when it\u0027s not. Presubmits are not enough, because they can only show the presence of a bug, but not an absence of them and I\u0027d rather we not open ourselves up to subtle behavior differences depending on whether $OUT_DIR is set or not.\n\nIt would be nice if there was an object testing code (but only testing code) had access to which could house this method. I\u0027m afraid I\u0027m not familiar enough with the testing framework to suggest how that could be achieved 😞",
      "parentUuid": "c9f6f630_06af063a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 191,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 191,
        "endChar": 32
      },
